WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
Edited app screenshots
Synthetic narration

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:10.048
BioGraph Steward helps scientists ask a protein question, see an evidence
graph, and check the sources without writing graph queries.

00:00:10.048 --> 00:00:13.373
One application provides two saved examples.

00:00:13.373 --> 00:00:16.623
We begin in the Added source context workspace.

00:00:16.623 --> 00:00:20.145
The hosted demonstration needs no account or running model.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.579
Pharos supplies the backbone.

00:00:23.579 --> 00:00:30.329
Native Gene Ontology location records and sequence-checked STRING
associations add traceable context.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:38.329
For KRAS and CDC42BPB, the source passport shows an association absent from
captured Pharos.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:43.853
Its provider, original record, identity checks and candidate status remain
visible.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:52.659
A published human-location benchmark matches 31 of the 99 targets, with 51
known location labels.

00:00:52.659 --> 00:00:58.109
Native annotations recover 44, compared with 41 for captured Pharos.

00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:04.059
Some observations are shared with the Human Protein Atlas, limiting
independent confirmation.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:09.197
OpenCell imaging supplies a separate, previously used research sensitivity
check.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:15.576
Nemotron selects a supported source tool, such as the STRING association
reader.

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:22.451
It matches the protein to the loaded cohort, checks the attached sources,
and validates the query arguments.

00:01:22.451 --> 00:01:27.426
The agent inspects selected citations and proposes review actions.

00:01:27.426 --> 00:01:32.957
This recorded investigation shows 8 of 14 matching proteins under its saved
limit.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.865
Open the manual reader for all 14 returned partners.

00:01:37.865 --> 00:01:40.715
Graph view focuses an individual result.

00:01:40.715 --> 00:01:43.240
Show all results restores the overview.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.565
Type a start entity and choose a connected destination.

00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:54.140
Try KRAS to CDC42BPB, TP53 to nucleus, or BRAF to a pathway.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.101
Results and evaluation explains the comparisons.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:05.044
For the demonstration, download the editable KRAS copy, extract it and run
its Python launcher.

00:02:05.044 --> 00:02:08.944
It includes the application, graph and preserved sources.

00:02:08.944 --> 00:02:14.024
Choose a claim, enter a reviewer, decision and reason, then save a new run.

00:02:14.024 --> 00:02:15.949
The original is preserved.

00:02:15.949 --> 00:02:18.043
The shared website stays read-only.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:22.990
A separate historical study tests protein function prediction.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:27.990
LocalPlus is a published method that transfers known functions from
connected proteins.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:32.190
A learned model combines network, sequence and annotation context.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.215
Fmax summarizes the precision-recall balance.

00:02:35.215 --> 00:02:38.665
Higher is better; this is not percentage accuracy.

00:02:38.665 --> 00:02:47.965
In the primary evaluation of 1,954 proteins, it rises from 0.055 to 0.073.

00:02:47.965 --> 00:02:53.740
The sensitivity view rises from 0.172 to 0.210.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:58.390
Paired intervals support both gains over retained LocalPlus within this
study.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.815
Extra gain beyond refreshed annotations remains uncertain.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.399
The Qualified Pharos workspace demonstrates recorded graph decisions.

00:03:08.399 --> 00:03:18.324
It excludes 298 records with obsolete Gene Ontology identifiers and retains
16,687 records.

00:03:18.324 --> 00:03:25.383
Every decision preserves its reason and original input, so the retained
graph remains inspectable and recoverable.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:34.744
Source additions, location-label recovery, graph qualification and
historical prediction answer different questions.

00:03:34.744 --> 00:03:43.333
The app keeps their evidence and controls visible, so scientists can
understand what each result supports and decide what to inspect next.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.914
Explore the hosted application without signing in.

00:03:47.914 --> 00:03:55.939
The final handoff contains the report, this demonstration, slides, and one
clearly indexed app and graph package.

00:03:55.939 --> 00:04:02.319
Build a scoped cohort locally, or use a saved example to follow a question
all the way to its evidence.
